Q2. Write a python program to accept a file name from user. If file exist display contents of file and number of characters, words and lines in a file, otherwise display appropriate message.

[20 Marks]

# Q2 Alternative Solution

filename = input("Enter file name: ")

try:
    with open(filename, 'r') as file:
        content = file.read()

        print("\nFile Contents:\n")
        print(content)

        # Count characters
        char_count = len(content)

        # Count words
        word_count = len(content.split())

        # Count lines
        line_count = content.count('\n') + 1

        print("\nNumber of characters:", char_count)
        print("Number of words:", word_count)
        print("Number of lines:", line_count)

except FileNotFoundError:
    print("Error: File does not exist!")


